      "id": "s01-canada-westminster-federal-framework-reuse-descriptions-0",
      "entityId": "canada-westminster-federal-framework",
      "category": "overview",
      "value": "The 1931 statute removed repugnancy restrictions and required Canadian request and consent for later UK legislation. It preserved the British North America Acts amendment exception. The earlier bicameral federal structure continued; later constitutional patriation and modern representation counts are excluded.",
